  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Vox’s core royalty operations are benefiting from strong momentum and extended mine lives, such as the Bonikro gold mine now projected through 2036, which improves cash flow visibility. The portfolio is gold-focused, where producer activity reinforces revenue durability. The shares trade at a marked discount to peers on a per-royalty-ounce basis, hinting at underappreciated asset quality.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management raised full-year guidance, initiated a quarterly dividend, and set a 2030 royalty receipt target, demonstrating confidence and a shareholder-return mindset. The company is debt-free with an undrawn credit line, preserving strategic flexibility. Growing institutional ownership and a new Buy-rated analyst initiation add external validation to management’s plan.",
